From 9045bb24553d49c2cce2cf6000b697faafca284f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Gamb <nick.gamb@solo.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:02:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(ateapi): a pool with its own ServiceAccount only runs
 its namespace's actors

Worker selectors match worker labels across namespaces, so an ActorTemplate
anywhere can select any pool whose labels it names. With pools running as a
workload identity (WorkerPoolPodTemplate.serviceAccountName) that would let
an actor borrow another namespace's identity.

AssignWorker now also requires that the worker's pool admits the template's
namespace: pools on the default ServiceAccount stay shareable across
namespaces (unchanged behavior); a pool with its own ServiceAccount admits
only templates in its own namespace. An unknown pool admits nothing from
other namespaces.
